# Project development

Before making any change in this repo, read and follow
`.claude/skills/project-development/SKILL.md`. It is the authoritative workflow
for developing and shipping this service onto the weisssrv k3s cluster: the
local loop, Flux debugging, and the secret / routing / observability
conventions.

Key standing rules (the skill has the detail):

- Flux owns all Kubernetes state under `kubernetes/flux/`. Never `kubectl apply`
  or `helm upgrade` to deploy — preview with `kustomize build kubernetes/flux`
  and deploy by merging.
- Never push to `main`; branch → merge request, always.
- Never commit secrets — reference them from `ExternalSecret` manifests.
- Containers stay non-root with a read-only root filesystem; no `latest` tags.
- Stay within your single namespace.
- CI comes in three shapes and this repo keeps one: `.gitlab-ci.yml` (shape
  `gitlab`, includes the shared `eric/weisssrv-lib` library at a pinned tag — do
  not re-inline it), `.github/workflows/` (shape `github`, a vendored
  equivalent), or neither (shape `none`, Flux-only). Check which is present
  before editing CI — see `docs/CI-SHAPES.md`.
- Scaffold with the `weisssrv-new-project` CLI; pick the CI shape with
  `./scripts/select-ci.sh` — see `docs/CONSUMING.md`.
